# Implementation Plan - Phase D: Precipitation Reliability Specialist (Gate 3 / P0)

Precipitation is explicitly central to the SIH problem statement and requires a real benchmarked reliability specialist rather than a UI label.
Phase D implements precipitation forecast failure estimation across occurrence, amount, threshold, heavy rain, extreme rain, timing, and spatial displacement across distinct accumulation windows (6h, 12h, 24h, 48h, 72h).

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Precipitation ≠ Flood**: The specialist diagnoses NWP precipitation forecast reliability; it does NOT predict flooding. Unsupported amount, timing, spatial, or extreme fields remain `null`.
> - **Anti-Leakage**: All precipitation features are strictly constrained to information available at issue time $t_0$. Ground truth observations (IMD gridded rainfall, GPM/IMERG) and post-valid-time corrections are sealed behind verification latency.
> - **Baseline Progression**: Every level of the baseline ladder (Climatology, Raw Ensemble, Spread Logistic, V3 + Precip Features, Continuous Error, Heavy-Rain Specialist, Spatial Challenger) is systematically benchmarked.

