### 1. Data Contracts & Manifests

#### [NEW] [precipitation_target_manifest.json](file:///c:/Users/adity/OneDrive/Desktop/SIH26079-RII/data/precipitation_target_manifest.json)
- Define canonical precipitation target definitions across accumulation intervals (6h, 12h, 24h, 48h, 72h).
- Standard IMD rainfall intensity thresholds:
  - Light (>2.5 mm)
  - Moderate (>15.6 mm)
  - Heavy (>64.5 mm)
  - Very Heavy (>115.5 mm)
  - Extremely Heavy (>204.4 mm)
- Target metrics:
  - Occurrence failure: False Alarm ($F \ge 2.5\text{mm}, O < 2.5\text{mm}$) and Miss ($F < 2.5\text{mm}, O \ge 2.5\text{mm}$)
  - Amount error: $|F - O| > \text{threshold}$ and continuous signed/absolute error
  - Heavy rain failure: Missed heavy rain ($O \ge 64.5\text{mm}, F < 64.5\text{mm}$) and False Alarm ($F \ge 64.5\text{mm}, O < 64.5\text{mm}$)
  - Extreme rain failure: $O \ge 204.4\text{mm}$ or $F \ge 204.4\text{mm}$
  - Timing displacement: Peak rainfall hour error $|\tau_F - \tau_O| > 6\text{h}$
  - Spatial displacement: Centroid position offset $D_{\text{centroid}} > 75\text{km}$

